From 55d7960517d08c1470f8c8491c0bf0cd5cd5d793 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 09:49:08 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Fetch publications automatically from OpenAlex; add
 members page

- data/members.json is now the single source for the members page and the
  publication fetch, holding each member's OpenAlex author id(s) and ORCID.
- scripts/fetch-publications.mjs queries OpenAlex per member, keeps CWI-affiliated
  work, merges each preprint with its published version, and writes
  data/publications.generated.json. No dependencies, no API key.
- .github/workflows/publications.yml refreshes that file weekly and on demand;
  Deploy.yml now also rebuilds on its completion, since a GITHUB_TOKEN push
  cannot re-trigger the push event.
- New /publications/all page renders the generated list with search, a per-member
  filter and a preprint toggle. The hand-written pages under /publications/ are
  untouched and are now the 'Selected publications' page; adding a doi: to their
  frontmatter links them from the generated list.
- New /members page, driven by data/members.json.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
